WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.459
[exciting rock music plays]

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.879
Ever since I was a kid,
I've always wanted to be a criminal.

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:08.341
If I could've put it in my yearbook,
I'd have put, "I wanna be a criminal."

00:00:10.218 --> 00:00:12.804
Things have changed. Nowadays
you gotta figure out some sort of way

00:00:12.887 --> 00:00:14.014
to finesse the system.

00:00:14.097 --> 00:00:15.432
My name is Raymond Trapani,

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.726
Chief Operating Officer of Centra Tech.

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:20.145
Our pitch to the world was that

00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:21.813
we were gonna create a debit card

00:00:21.896 --> 00:00:24.524
where you'd be able to spend
your cryptocurrency in real time.

00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:27.569
- It's an electronic money.
- Something about bitcoins or something.

00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:30.655
I was all about Centra Tech.
"Look at this, this makes sense."

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:34.492
Just watching something become
extremely valuable, it's like a drug.

00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:38.413
[Ray] Tons of money just starts
flooding in, 100,000, another 100,000.

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:41.416
It was probably the most exciting thing
I ever experienced in my life.

00:00:41.416 --> 00:00:43.293
[Ray] We didn't know
a thing about this business,

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:46.046
but it didn't matter at all.
It was too easy.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:47.255
[phone ringing]

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.632
[beeps]

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.217
[man 1] Ray, Visa's just saying

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:55.138
this company Centra is not allowed
to issue a card with "Visa" on it.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.891
[Ray] I-- I know--
I know details about that.

00:00:57.974 --> 00:01:00.226
I-- I can't give you
direct answers on that.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:03.104
- [intriguing music plays]
- [man 1] It just didn't make sense.

00:01:03.188 --> 00:01:04.355
Things looked funny.

00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:06.357
[man 2] They have nothing.

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:10.570
So the whole thing is to now make
themselves as legitimate as possible.

00:01:10.653 --> 00:01:12.405
[man 3] It was very suspicious.

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:15.784
I started noticing that
things were changing on their website.

00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:19.162
[man 1] The pictures didn't even
look like real people.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.039
[man 3] I researched the founders.

00:01:21.122 --> 00:01:25.085
Wow, the CEO is actually
Raymond's grandfather.

00:01:25.168 --> 00:01:27.796
[man 4] There was an aspect to Centra
that was really brazen.

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:30.840
We are 100% not a scam.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.384
No one ever says that
unless it's actually a scam.

00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:34.803
[laughs]

00:01:34.886 --> 00:01:38.431
[man 2] This shady company
just graduated to the next level.

00:01:39.015 --> 00:01:41.851
[man 4] They started taking actions
to try and hide things.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.853
Money started going out of accounts.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:47.148
[man 1] Somebody needs to figure out
what the hell is going on here.

00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:49.234
[man 3] I took a considerable loss.

00:01:49.317 --> 00:01:51.194
[man 5] Obviously,
something was not right.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.822
[man 6] It's like giving a middle finger
to the FBI.

00:01:53.905 --> 00:01:55.073
[man 7] He's a real criminal.

00:01:55.156 --> 00:01:56.574
[man 8] Ray's a piece of ****.

00:01:56.658 --> 00:01:58.409
[man 3] Absolutely wanted
to take them down.

00:01:58.493 --> 00:01:59.828
[man 9] This guy's a fraudster.

00:01:59.911 --> 00:02:01.412
[music crescendoes, ends]

